  "learning_notes": {
    "goal": "Study a roughly 2\u00d7 Keplerian beam expander and a four-surface, air-spaced lens assembly.",
    "start": "Use Top view at Z = 35 mm. Compare surface radii at telescope-1 and telescope-2; find focus after focusing-assembly.",
    "experiments": [
      "Move telescope-2 by \u00b15 mm along X to change output convergence.",
      "Change the internal air gap in focusing-assembly from 10 to 5 or 20 mm.",
      "Swap one singlet material and compare chromatic focal shift.",
      "Reduce an internal clear aperture to see clipping at that interface."
    ],
    "limit": "The telescope spacing makes its first-order C term vanish at 780 nm. Finite rays retain spherical/chromatic aberrations. The 150 mm doublet is an illustrative scaled prescription."
